  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is Comet Halley's orbital period in months? Comet Halley orbits the sun every 76 years. Comet Halley's appearances are treated as occurring exactly once every 75 years. One year is defined as 12 months.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Comet Halley’s orbital period is \\(76\\) years. Since \\(1\\) year equals \\(12\\) months:\n\n\\[\n76 \\times 12 = 912\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Comet Halley’s orbital period is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{912\\text{ months}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Comet Halley orbits the sun every 75 years.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Using the corrected orbital period of \\(75\\) years:\n\n\\[\n75 \\times 12 = 900\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Comet Halley’s orbital period is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{900\\text{ months}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many times would Comet Halley appear during Bill's 150-year lifetime? Additionally, Bill's lifetime lasts exactly 150 years.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill’s lifetime is \\(150\\) years, and Comet Halley appears once every \\(75\\) years.\n\n\\[\n\\frac{150}{75}=2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Comet Halley would appear during Bill’s lifetime:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ times}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Bill's father saw Comet Halley when he was 32 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill’s father seeing Comet Halley at age \\(32\\) does not change the calculation for Bill’s lifetime. Since Bill lived exactly \\(150\\) years and the comet appears every \\(75\\) years:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{150}{75}=2\n\\]\n\nThus, assuming the lifetime spans two complete 75-year intervals, Comet Halley would appear:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\text{ times}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How old was Bill when he saw Comet Halley for the first time? One more thing you should know: Bill saw Comet Halley a second time when he was three times the age his father was when his father saw Comet Halley.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill’s father was \\(32\\) years old when he saw Comet Halley. Bill saw it a second time at three times that age:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 32 = 96\n\\]\n\nSince Comet Halley appears every \\(75\\) years, Bill’s first sighting was:\n\n\\[\n96 - 75 = 21\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Bill was\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{21\\text{ years old}}\n\\]\n\nwhen he saw Comet Halley for the first time.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — Bill is alive for the entire 150-year period being considered.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill saw Comet Halley a second time at:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 32 = 96\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nBecause the comet appears every \\(75\\) years, his first sighting was:\n\n\\[\n96 - 75 = 21\n\\]\n\nBill being alive for the entire \\(150\\)-year period does not change this. Therefore, Bill was\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{21\\text{ years old}}\n\\]\n\nwhen he saw Comet Halley for the first time.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Bill's father saw Comet Halley when he was 30 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Bill’s father saw Comet Halley at age \\(30\\). Bill saw it a second time at:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 30 = 90\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nSince Comet Halley appears every \\(75\\) years, Bill’s first sighting was:\n\n\\[\n90 - 75 = 15\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Bill was\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{15\\text{ years old}}\n\\]\n\nwhen he saw Comet Halley for the first time.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
